WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.900
This is a transformer, simplified,
and read from the bottom up.

2
00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:08.000
The phrase small red bird goes in.

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.675
At the top comes a prediction
for the next word.

4
00:00:11.875 --> 00:00:19.350
In between, almost every step is
linear algebra: vectors, dot products,

5
00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:21.925
and matrix products.

6
00:00:22.125 --> 00:00:26.800
Let's see where the linear algebra
is, and the one place it stops.

7
00:00:27.967 --> 00:00:30.342
Focus on the last position, bird.

8
00:00:30.342 --> 00:00:33.517
Its query vector, q, is one, one.

9
00:00:33.717 --> 00:00:36.162
Each position also has a key.

10
00:00:36.162 --> 00:00:38.186
Small has key one, zero.

11
00:00:38.186 --> 00:00:40.442
Red has key zero, one.

12
00:00:40.442 --> 00:00:43.242
And bird has key one, one.

13
00:00:43.442 --> 00:00:47.767
The relevance score is the dot
product of the query with each key:

14
00:00:47.767 --> 00:00:51.117
multiply matching entries, and add.

15
00:00:51.517 --> 00:00:56.242
For small: one times one,
plus one times zero, is one.

16
00:00:56.642 --> 00:01:01.742
For red: one times zero, plus
one times one, is also one.

17
00:01:02.142 --> 00:01:06.692
For bird: one times one,
plus one times one, is two.

18
00:01:07.392 --> 00:01:08.203
Geometrically,

19
00:01:08.203 --> 00:01:11.214
the dot product is the length
of the query times the

20
00:01:11.214 --> 00:01:15.142
signed length of the key's
shadow on the query's line.

21
00:01:15.342 --> 00:01:17.473
Small and red cast short shadows.

22
00:01:17.473 --> 00:01:23.117
Bird lies along the query, so its shadow
is longest, and it scores highest.

23
00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:30.150
To turn scores into weights, divide
each score by their sum, four.

24
00:01:30.850 --> 00:01:34.900
The weights are one quarter,
one quarter, and one half.

25
00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:38.750
They are nonnegative, and they add to one.

26
00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:45.200
Later, softmax replaces this rule, and
its weights have the same two properties.

27
00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:53.100
Each position also carries a value vector:
four, zero; zero, four; and four, four.

28
00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:59.675
The output for bird is the weighted average
of the values: one quarter of the first,

29
00:01:59.675 --> 00:02:02.400
plus one quarter of the second,

30
00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:04.975
plus one half of the third.

31
00:02:04.975 --> 00:02:07.425
That is three, three.

32
00:02:07.825 --> 00:02:11.012
Because the weights are
nonnegative and add to one,

33
00:02:11.012 --> 00:02:15.875
the output is a mix of the values,
inside the triangle they form.

34
00:02:17.767 --> 00:02:23.167
Every position does this at once, and
matrix products keep track of it all.

35
00:02:23.167 --> 00:02:28.092
First, stack the token vectors
as the rows of one matrix, X.

36
00:02:28.492 --> 00:02:31.617
X has one row per position.

37
00:02:32.017 --> 00:02:37.192
The queries come from a linear
map: Q equals X times W Q.

38
00:02:37.392 --> 00:02:40.359
Each entry of a matrix
product is a dot product:

39
00:02:40.359 --> 00:02:43.942
a row on the left with
a column on the right.

40
00:02:44.642 --> 00:02:48.792
So row i of Q is the query for position i.

41
00:02:49.192 --> 00:02:53.942
The keys and values come the same
way, from their own matrices.

42
00:02:54.642 --> 00:02:59.442
Next, the score matrix S
equals Q times K transpose.

43
00:02:59.642 --> 00:03:05.142
The rows of Q are the queries, and the
columns of K transpose are the keys.

44
00:03:05.342 --> 00:03:11.042
So the entry in row i, column j is the
dot product of query i with key j.

45
00:03:11.742 --> 00:03:15.067
Every score, in one matrix product.

46
00:03:15.067 --> 00:03:19.467
The bird row is one, one,
two: the scores we computed.

47
00:03:20.167 --> 00:03:24.217
Turning each row into weights
gives the weight matrix.

48
00:03:24.217 --> 00:03:28.142
Every row is nonnegative and adds to one.

49
00:03:28.542 --> 00:03:32.542
Finally, H equals the
weight matrix times V.

50
00:03:32.742 --> 00:03:37.642
Row i of H is position i's
weighted average of the rows of V.

51
00:03:38.042 --> 00:03:42.317
For bird, it is three, three,
the same point as before.

52
00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.292
So far, every step looks linear.

53
00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:50.025
But the weighting rule used
in practice is softmax:

54
00:03:50.025 --> 00:03:54.375
exponentiate each score,
then divide by the total.

55
00:03:55.075 --> 00:03:58.439
Treat attention as a
function of the query,

56
00:03:58.439 --> 00:04:02.525
F of q, with K and V from Activity 3.5.26.

57
00:04:02.925 --> 00:04:06.200
Multiplying q by K gives three scores.

58
00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:08.750
That step is linear.

59
00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:12.178
Softmax turns the scores
into a weight vector,

60
00:04:12.178 --> 00:04:17.125
a point in the triangle with
corners e one, e two, and e three.

61
00:04:17.325 --> 00:04:20.550
Watch the weights as the query moves.

62
00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:26.500
That step is not linear.

63
00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:32.425
Multiplying by V transpose sends this
triangle onto the value triangle.

64
00:04:32.425 --> 00:04:34.750
Linear again.

65
00:04:36.633 --> 00:04:39.133
Now the square grid test.

66
00:04:39.133 --> 00:04:44.183
A linear map keeps grid lines
straight, parallel, and evenly spaced.

67
00:04:46.383 --> 00:04:49.183
Push the same grid through F.

68
00:04:52.383 --> 00:04:57.558
The lines bend, crowd toward the edges,
and squeeze inside the triangle.

69
00:04:58.258 --> 00:04:59.335
One more check.

70
00:04:59.335 --> 00:05:02.433
A linear map sends zero to zero.

71
00:05:02.633 --> 00:05:06.283
But F of zero is one third, one third.

72
00:05:07.483 --> 00:05:11.183
Softmax is the step that breaks linearity.

73
00:05:13.067 --> 00:05:16.792
Here is the whole computation in one line.

74
00:05:16.792 --> 00:05:19.592
Stack the tokens into X.

75
00:05:19.592 --> 00:05:24.842
Multiply by three matrices to get
the queries, keys, and values.

76
00:05:25.042 --> 00:05:30.392
Multiply Q by K transpose, and
every score is a dot product.

77
00:05:30.592 --> 00:05:33.482
Apply softmax to each
row to get the weights.

78
00:05:33.482 --> 00:05:36.017
This is the nonlinear step.

79
00:05:36.417 --> 00:05:40.667
Multiply the weights by
V to average the values.

80
00:05:40.867 --> 00:05:46.017
That is attention: dot products,
matrix products, and one softmax.

81
00:05:46.217 --> 00:05:51.692
The other block in each layer, the small
neural network, gets its own video.
